{
  "0": "Change only sequence modeling: shorten the current maximum causal context to max(1, floor(0.75 * current_length)), retaining the most recent interactions in chronological order. Apply the same truncation during training and prediction. Removing older context may reduce stale-interest interference and recurrent computation. Preserve features, embeddings, GRU topology, readout, loss and optimizer across all four datasets.",
  "1": "Change only learning objective: retain the current loss and add 0.1 * mean(softplus(s_negative - s_positive)) over the existing valid positive/negative training pairs, without drawing additional negatives. This modest pairwise term may improve candidate ordering for HR@10. Preserve sampling, features, embeddings, GRU, scoring, optimizer, scheduler and training settings; train one model per dataset.",
  "2": "Change only feature construction: multiply each existing input embedding by 1/sqrt(1 + 0.1*c), where c counts earlier occurrences of that item in the available causal prefix. Exclude padding and never include the target. This deterministic feature may damp repetitive bursts that otherwise dominate recurrent state. Preserve learned embedding design, GRU, readout, loss and optimizer; reproduce the feature identically at prediction for all four datasets.",
  "3": "Change only network architecture: add a residual bypass around the existing GRU, using output_t = GRU_output_t + 0.1*P(input_embedding_t), with identity P when dimensions match and a jointly trained bias-free linear projection otherwise. Feed this output through the unchanged history readout and scorer. The bypass may preserve immediate item information alongside recurrent memory with little additional computation. Keep features, embeddings, history policy, loss and optimizer fixed; use one model per dataset."
}
